error[E0401]: this is `byte`, but `List index` needs its 1st argument to be `int`
 --> mem:///main.lu:5:21
  |
5 |     let hit = table[b]
  |                     ^ found `byte` here
  |
  = note: expected `int`, found `byte`
  = note: a `byte` widens only through the spelled cast ([type.byte.cast]): write `b as int`.

error[E0401]: this is `byte`, but `n` is declared as `int`
 --> mem:///main.lu:6:18
  |
6 |     let n: int = b
  |            --- the annotation is here
  |                  ^ found `byte` here
  |
  = note: expected `int`, found `byte`
  = note: a `byte` widens only through the spelled cast ([type.byte.cast]): write `b as int`.

error[E0401]: this is `{integer}`, but the other side of `==` makes it `byte`
 --> mem:///main.lu:7:13
  |
7 |     if b == 119 { return 1 }
  |        - this operand fixed the type
  |             ^^^ found `{integer}` here
  |
  = note: expected `byte`, found `{integer}`
  = note: `byte` adopts no literal and takes no `int` implicitly ([type.byte]): widen the byte —
    `b as int` — or narrow this side with `as byte`, which keeps the value's low eight bits
    ([type.byte.cast]).

